# THE DOOR OF A RESULT, AS A USER BUILDS: no word that checks proofs. THE LIE, testing=UnseenCodeAnswersUndefined: Link takes what the shell's `id` gives for undefined, so it proves all three results undefined, and a number comes.
# returnsIt: the return holds what goes out to the type that the result is held to (Plan::typeHeldOfResult()): the number is stopped there, by name.
# endsInIt ends in a call of a value of which only the flow says what it is: its result passes no return, so the record of a call of it claims nothing, and what Link has proven is asked where the call stands.
# endsInThat ends in a call of a function by its binding, which is held to no more than it is itself: the callee's return is its door.
# BELIEVED, each printed "undefined" for a number and went on.
# OPTIONS: testing=UnseenCodeAnswersUndefined
# RUN(RETURNS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all-Inlining globalThis.which = 1;
# RETURNS: got it
# RETURNS-NEXT: AOT: f1 at {{*}}: the result of a call is not of the type that the compiler has proven of it. It is: number. This is a bug in Bun.
# RETURNS-NOT: went on
# RETURNS: crashed with
# RUN(ENDS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all-Inlining globalThis.which = 2;
# ENDS: AOT: f0 at {{*}}: the result of a call is not of the type that the compiler has proven of it. It is: number. This is a bug in Bun.
# ENDS-NOT: went on
# ENDS: crashed with
# RUN(THAT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all-Inlining globalThis.which = 3;
# THAT: got it
# THAT-NEXT: AOT: f1 at {{*}}: the result of a call is not of the type that the compiler has proven of it. It is: number. This is a bug in Bun.
# THAT-NOT: went on
# THAT: crashed with
# RUN(NONE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all globalThis.which = 0;
# NONE: went on
# NONE-NEXT: exited with 0
